26. Rxc6 $16 { This is one of White’s dream positions in the hedgehog. The a6- and a4-pawns are nearly lost while Black cannot easily organize any counterplay. } Qb7 $6 { Aiming to trap the rook for two pieces, but this does not help. } ( { More stubborn was } 26... Bb6 27. Qxd6 Bxg1 28. Kxg1 Qa7 29. Kh1 Nb8 $1 { protecting the a6-pawn, though after } 30. Rxc8 Rxc8 31. Rc1 $1 { ± White still has a big advantage. } ) 
