 { Black is insisting on the threat of } g5-g4 { , and now White does not seem to have any useful moves since preventing the break with 21.g4?! weakens the dark squares, and after } Ne5 $15 { Black’s position is preferable. } ) 
g4 { White’s position now becomes unpleasant. } 21. hxg4 ( { Black is also doing well after } 21. h4 $5 gxf3 22. Nxf3 Rg6 $15 { when Black’s chances are preferable at least on a practical level. Controlling the e5-square and the g-file are dreams for hedgehog players. } ) 
hxg4 22. Bg5 $2 { White’s hopes for kingside activity are destined to fail. } ( { Much better was } 22. f4 $1 { keeping the g-file closed: } Nxe4 ( { or } 22. Bg5 Bxe4 $5 23. Nxe4 Nxe4 24. Qb2 Kh7 25. Bd3 Qb7 26. Qe2 $13 ) 
 ( { PH: } 22. Bg5 Rg7 $5 { is the computer's move, combining defense with attacking ideas on the h-file. } ) 
